import LeanDring.P5.Certificate.ConjugacyClasses.Twin1.NormLink1
import LeanDring.P5.Certificate.Characters.Twin1.CharAssembly

/-!
# Normalizer generators and the matrix-realization checkers

For each of the 148 subgroup-class representatives `H = reps r` (echelon basis
`B = getB (classRepsData r) = basisAt r`), the generator
`LeanDring/P5/Certificate/Generators/Twin1/NormGen.lean` emits the conjugation matrices
`normMats r` as `expVec`s of conjugation **by the generators of `normBasis B`**
— an echelon base of `N_G(H)` sifted out of `G`. Those generators need not be
the canonical inventory base `getB (normIdxData r)` that `NormCard.lean`
identifies as `N_G(H)`, so the matrices cannot be checked against that base
directly.

They are instead certified against **their own** generating set. This file
embeds `normGens r` — the `normBasis B` coordinate elements, in the same outer
order as `normMats r` — and provides four kernel checkers, discharged
whole-range in the sibling `NormLink.lean`:

* `normGenMemCheck` — each `n ∈ normGens r` sifts into `getB (normIdxData r)`,
  i.e. lies in `N_G(reps r)`;
* `normGenWfCheck` — `normGens r` is a well-formed echelon base (`wfB'`), so its
  closure has order `5 ^ (normGens r).length`;
* `normGenLenCheck` — `(normGens r).length = (getB (normIdxData r)).length`, so
  that order equals `|N_G(reps r)|` and the closure is all of `N_G(reps r)`;
* `normRealizeCheck` — `normMats r = (normGens r).map (conjMatrixL2 B)`, the
  per-entry realization `(normMats r)[j][i] = expVec_B (nⱼ⁻¹ · gᵢ · nⱼ)` with
  `nⱼ = (normGens r)[j]`, `gᵢ = B[i]`.

Orientation (as emitted by `NormGen.conjMatrix`): row `i` of `nⱼ`'s matrix is
`expVec B (conjC 1 (invC 1 nⱼ) gᵢ) = expVec_B (nⱼ⁻¹ gᵢ nⱼ)` — conjugation is
`n⁻¹ g n`.
-/

namespace LeanDring.P5Presentation

open Fin.NatCast

set_option maxRecDepth 100000

